WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.339
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:04.609 --> 00:05.902
You bastard!

3
00:18.248 --> 00:20.125
I'll kill them all at once.

4
00:34.597 --> 00:36.266
Everyone, we're leaving the village.

5
00:39.853 --> 00:41.896
Sanada!

6
00:46.651 --> 00:48.319
Feel the weight of the lives…

7
00:50.572 --> 00:51.990
you've taken!

8
01:10.383 --> 01:12.635
Her Ladyship, Lady Yodo.

9
01:17.390 --> 01:18.892
Raise your heads.

10
01:40.163 --> 01:41.247
Nobushige…

11
01:41.748 --> 01:43.249
LADY YODO

12
01:43.333 --> 01:45.335
You're the only one I can count on.

13
01:54.010 --> 01:55.595
What's Osaka like?

14
01:56.179 --> 01:59.599
I hear you can get a delicious Western food called tempura there.

15
01:59.682 --> 02:00.850
Is that true?

16
02:00.934 --> 02:02.185
Tempura?

17
02:03.061 --> 02:04.604
You keep yapping about that.

18
02:04.687 --> 02:06.314
What can you expect?

19
02:06.397 --> 02:08.316
He has never left the village before.

20
02:08.900 --> 02:09.901
I see…

21
02:11.069 --> 02:13.696
The Miyoshi brothers are from Osaka, right?

22
02:13.780 --> 02:17.492
Yes. It was a lively, wonderful city. Back in the Toyotomi days.

23
02:17.575 --> 02:20.119
Seikai ran an apothecary there.

24
02:21.329 --> 02:22.622
I hope you can do it again.

25
02:22.705 --> 02:23.539
I hope so.

26
02:24.082 --> 02:26.626
Then you should open a restaurant too.

27
02:27.627 --> 02:28.544
That sounds good!

28
02:28.628 --> 02:30.380
You just want free food.

29
02:31.047 --> 02:32.382
All right, everyone!

30
02:36.552 --> 02:39.597
At this rate, we'll reach Osaka Castle by tomorrow.

31
02:39.681 --> 02:43.935
That Tsuge ninja is looking for us, isn't he?

32
02:45.311 --> 02:47.438
If we keep heading north,

33
02:47.522 --> 02:51.234
there's only one bridge across the river.

34
02:51.776 --> 02:55.363
Once we've crossed, we can destroy the bridge and buy ourselves some time.

35
02:56.531 --> 02:57.365
Right.

36
02:59.409 --> 03:00.410
Are we on the right road?

37
03:01.327 --> 03:02.495
Let me see.

38
03:02.996 --> 03:05.081
Hey, aren't those two a little too close?

39
03:05.873 --> 03:08.710
Kirigakure Saizo and Yuri Kamanosuke.

40
03:08.793 --> 03:11.421
They've been together since they were kids.

41
03:12.088 --> 03:15.299
There's no room for you to get between them.

42
03:16.050 --> 03:17.552
Let's take a break.

43
03:17.635 --> 03:19.220
-Yes, let's take a break here. -Yes.

44
03:19.303 --> 03:22.265
Hey, Yuri. Why do you go by Kamanosuke?

45
03:24.392 --> 03:25.727
None of your business.

46
03:25.810 --> 03:27.311
I wasn't asking you.

47
03:28.563 --> 03:30.481
North's that way. We're on the right track.

48
03:31.399 --> 03:34.777
Come to think of it, I never heard you thank me.

49
03:34.861 --> 03:35.778
What?

50
03:35.862 --> 03:38.156
You got out of the village thanks to me.

51
03:38.239 --> 03:40.074
All you did was climb a tree, monkey.

52
03:40.158 --> 03:41.701
What'd you say?

53
03:41.784 --> 03:42.618
No, no…

54
03:42.702 --> 03:46.122
We got out of the village thanks to Kakei.

55
03:46.205 --> 03:47.248
I'm grateful.

56
03:47.332 --> 03:48.166
KAKEI JUZO

57
03:48.249 --> 03:50.710
Even with 100 arrows, you'd miss, Mochizuki.

58
03:51.836 --> 03:53.463
And he's coming with us too.

59
03:54.047 --> 03:57.467
Ieyasu has killed many of my comrades.

60
04:00.595 --> 04:02.472
I'll do what I can

61
04:03.431 --> 04:05.266
to honor them.

62
04:10.146 --> 04:11.814
Leave the support to me.

63
04:12.565 --> 04:13.483
Much appreciated!

64
04:13.566 --> 04:16.778
Hey! I'm the one who brought Kakei along.

65
04:16.861 --> 04:20.656
That makes me the best of the bunch. Right, old man Yukimura?

66
04:20.740 --> 04:21.783
That's right.

67
04:21.866 --> 04:22.867
Don't encourage him.

68
04:22.950 --> 04:24.619
He'll only get cockier.

69
04:24.702 --> 04:27.205
Wait, what did you even do?

70
04:27.288 --> 04:29.540
Shut up if you did nothing.

71
04:30.458 --> 04:31.292
What?

72
04:31.376 --> 04:32.335
"What?"

73
04:32.418 --> 04:34.170
You stand before our lord!

74
04:34.253 --> 04:36.089
Enough, you two!

75
04:46.015 --> 04:47.225
There's something we have

76
04:48.351 --> 04:49.727
that the Tokugawa don't.

77
04:51.396 --> 04:52.313
Our bonds.

78
04:53.564 --> 04:54.732
To Ieyasu,

79
04:55.817 --> 04:58.277
his retainers are nothing but disposable tools.

80
05:02.698 --> 05:03.616
And that…

81
05:04.283 --> 05:05.368
is precisely

82
05:06.077 --> 05:07.412
their weakness.

83
05:09.163 --> 05:10.832
Our bonds, huh…

84
05:11.582 --> 05:13.501
Bound together, we can never be severed.

85
05:14.335 --> 05:15.420
Just like this cord.

86
05:32.228 --> 05:35.648
Well, I'm amazing even on my own.

87
05:39.610 --> 05:40.486
Shit…

88
05:43.656 --> 05:44.699
You frustrated?

89
05:46.492 --> 05:47.326
Shit.

90
05:48.452 --> 05:49.370
You're stepping on it.

91
05:52.373 --> 05:53.624
Gross!

92
05:53.708 --> 05:55.293
It's deer droppings!

93
05:55.918 --> 05:57.795
Kakei! Look!

94
05:57.879 --> 06:00.173
Yukimura has left Kudoyama?

95
06:00.256 --> 06:01.090
Yes, my lord.

96
06:01.174 --> 06:02.633
What a disgrace!

97
06:03.134 --> 06:04.177
You fool!

98
06:04.886 --> 06:07.221
You fool! Raise your head!

99
06:13.144 --> 06:14.103
Seize him.

100
06:17.023 --> 06:20.943
Under no circumstances can we let Yukimura enter Osaka Castle.

101
06:27.158 --> 06:28.951
Where is the ninja?

102
06:29.035 --> 06:29.869
Speak!

103
06:30.494 --> 06:31.454
Speak!

104
06:35.333 --> 06:36.709
A villager claims

105
06:37.710 --> 06:39.295
one of the ninja

106
06:40.213 --> 06:43.007
flew up to that watchtower.

107
06:43.090 --> 06:45.092
It was likely Sasuke.

108
06:46.177 --> 06:47.178
Sasuke?

109
06:48.221 --> 06:50.014
What shall we do with the villagers?

110
06:51.224 --> 06:52.850
Burn the entire village to the ground.

111
06:54.227 --> 06:56.604
It's Ogosho's order.

112
06:58.439 --> 06:59.273
Yes, my lord.

113
07:08.950 --> 07:09.784
What?

114
07:10.576 --> 07:11.536
What's wrong?

115
07:13.496 --> 07:14.872
The bridge is gone.

116
07:15.831 --> 07:17.500
It should be right here!

117
07:18.292 --> 07:20.795
The heavy rains last month must've washed it away.

118
07:22.797 --> 07:24.882
So, what do we do now?

119
07:24.966 --> 07:26.133
Is there another way across?

120
07:26.717 --> 07:27.927
No.

121
07:28.010 --> 07:30.304
We'll have to backtrack and find another route.

122
07:30.388 --> 07:33.140
We have to go all the way back?

123
07:34.642 --> 07:35.685
That's right!

124
07:37.395 --> 07:39.522
I came prepared for just such an occasion.

125
07:39.605 --> 07:43.025
If we tie this to the opposite bank, we should be able to cross.

126
07:43.734 --> 07:46.946
Not bad. That's Sanada's strategist for you.

127
07:47.029 --> 07:48.406
How long is it?

128
07:48.489 --> 07:50.658
Well… 25 ken.

129
07:52.702 --> 07:54.662
It's 30 ken to the other bank.

130
07:54.745 --> 07:56.163
So it's useless.

131
07:56.789 --> 07:57.832
I take it back.

132
08:01.711 --> 08:03.129
Okuni gave this to me.

133
08:04.463 --> 08:06.966
Here. I wove this with all my heart.

134
08:07.049 --> 08:09.051
I'm sure it'll protect you, Sasuke.

135
08:12.430 --> 08:16.225
Even with the knots, it's 35 ken long. This will work.

136
08:16.309 --> 08:17.685
-Great. -I take it back!

137
08:17.768 --> 08:19.020
Look at you, Master Strategist!

138
08:20.771 --> 08:21.939
What's wrong, Seikai?

139
08:22.898 --> 08:24.233
We can't cross this river.

140
08:25.985 --> 08:29.113
Brother's afraid of water. He nearly drowned when he was little.

141
08:31.073 --> 08:32.158
Sorry…

142
08:32.950 --> 08:34.076
I can't do this.

143
08:35.995 --> 08:37.705
He's the worst.

144
08:37.788 --> 08:40.541
I mean, how are we even supposed to get the rope to the other bank?

145
08:43.044 --> 08:44.211
Well…

146
08:45.338 --> 08:46.839
I take it back.

147
08:47.590 --> 08:48.924
What shall we do, my lord?

148
08:50.968 --> 08:51.802
We'll take a detour.

149
08:51.886 --> 08:53.387
What?!

150
08:56.724 --> 08:58.184
You…

151
08:59.435 --> 09:01.103
Let's just eat first.

152
09:01.937 --> 09:04.106
An army marches on its stomach.

153
09:04.190 --> 09:06.275
Like we have any food!

154
09:06.984 --> 09:07.818
Hey.

155
09:08.736 --> 09:09.570
We do.

156
09:10.446 --> 09:12.406
You're the best!

157
09:13.282 --> 09:14.492
This place is dangerous.

158
09:14.575 --> 09:17.745
There's an abandoned village to the east where we can hide.

159
09:17.828 --> 09:18.996
This is good.

160
09:21.582 --> 09:22.708
Something's coming.

161
09:23.918 --> 09:26.253
Lord Yukimura! Over here!

162
09:30.383 --> 09:32.927
Tsuge… He's already here…

163
09:36.430 --> 09:37.264
That idiot!

164
09:37.348 --> 09:39.517
You're the bastard who killed Unno!

165
09:48.401 --> 09:49.360
Sasuke!

166
09:55.658 --> 09:57.910
Found you.

167
10:00.496 --> 10:03.457
Bind, Secure, Conceal, Ironize.

168
10:15.344 --> 10:16.762
The bullets aren't doing anything…

169
10:16.846 --> 10:18.222
Over here!

170
10:18.305 --> 10:20.641
Ninja Art: Flame Release!

171
10:45.499 --> 10:46.500
Saizo!

172
10:58.345 --> 10:59.430
Yuri!

173
10:59.513 --> 11:01.223
Stay out of my way.

174
11:07.897 --> 11:09.315
Mist Concealment.

175
11:09.398 --> 11:10.357
MIST CONCEALMENT

176
11:12.026 --> 11:13.569
Now! Run!

177
11:30.336 --> 11:31.253
Mother!

178
11:32.505 --> 11:35.466
I hear you leaked Iga's secrets to outsiders.

179
11:37.051 --> 11:38.385
By order of the code,

180
11:39.053 --> 11:40.137
you must die.

181
11:40.221 --> 11:41.931
Please spare my child!

182
11:50.523 --> 11:51.607
Father!

183
11:53.275 --> 11:54.360
Saizo.

184
11:55.027 --> 11:56.237
You do it.

185
12:02.451 --> 12:03.744
Saizo…

186
12:24.390 --> 12:25.975
Letting emotions control you?

187
12:27.101 --> 12:28.727
You're no ninja.

188
12:44.743 --> 12:47.246
If you do this, you'll be…

189
12:49.164 --> 12:50.124
Yuri…

190
12:52.626 --> 12:53.502
Are you hurt?

191
12:54.670 --> 12:56.213
Nothing serious.

192
13:20.613 --> 13:22.448
-Saizo? -You're awake.

193
13:23.324 --> 13:24.158
Are you hurt?

194
13:25.326 --> 13:26.452
Nothing serious.

195
13:27.661 --> 13:29.288
I'm sorry. This is all my fault.

196
13:33.042 --> 13:34.460
I won't let you die.

197
13:37.463 --> 13:38.297
Nothing.

198
13:38.839 --> 13:39.673
You two.

199
13:41.091 --> 13:42.051
Where are the others?

200
13:43.594 --> 13:44.720
We got separated.

201
13:46.472 --> 13:48.682
Let's head for the abandoned village Anayama mentioned.

202
14:01.445 --> 14:03.739
Okuni! Okuni!

203
14:04.782 --> 14:07.409
Okuni! Hurry, run…

204
14:20.589 --> 14:21.590
Why…

205
14:22.549 --> 14:23.968
It's my orders.

206
14:24.051 --> 14:25.594
Lord Tsuge has apparently found

207
14:25.678 --> 14:27.930
Yukimura and his men at Zao Pass.

208
14:28.013 --> 14:29.348
-Let's go. -Yes, sir.

209
14:32.601 --> 14:36.105
Ready or not, here I come!

210
14:38.357 --> 14:40.150
You're late, all of you.

211
14:40.943 --> 14:44.363
Only Lord Hanzo can keep up with Lord Tsuge.

212
14:45.656 --> 14:48.033
Where's Yukimura?

213
14:49.201 --> 14:50.828
Still searching.

214
14:55.916 --> 14:59.795
Ready or not, here I come!

215
15:00.921 --> 15:02.006
Don't make a sound!

216
15:06.969 --> 15:08.804
They're close…

217
15:11.098 --> 15:14.184
If they were samurai, it'd be different. But capture even one ninja,

218
15:14.268 --> 15:16.687
and we can make him reveal Yukimura's location.

219
15:17.771 --> 15:20.607
That's all their comradeship amounts to.

220
15:30.617 --> 15:33.746
Found you.

221
15:38.208 --> 15:39.877
Where's Yukimura?

222
15:39.960 --> 15:42.046
How should I know?

223
15:42.629 --> 15:44.381
Tell me, and you'll be rewarded.

224
15:44.923 --> 15:45.966
A reward?

225
15:46.759 --> 15:47.968
No, really, I don't know.

226
15:54.099 --> 15:55.059
You're lying.

227
15:55.684 --> 15:56.727
Die!

228
16:01.523 --> 16:03.484
I give up! I know!

229
16:03.567 --> 16:04.526
I know!

230
16:05.110 --> 16:06.361
I'll take you to Yukimura!

231
16:18.457 --> 16:21.251
I hope Sasuke's all right.

232
16:22.044 --> 16:24.421
Now's no time to worry about him.

233
16:24.505 --> 16:27.132
They know we're in this area.

234
16:28.425 --> 16:30.010
The enemy is everywhere.

235
16:30.094 --> 16:31.512
They're searching for us in force.

236
16:33.097 --> 16:35.599
Hattori Hanzo is probably heading here too.

237
16:36.266 --> 16:38.560
If Hanzo and Tsuge join forces…

238
16:39.394 --> 16:40.229
it's over.

239
17:16.098 --> 17:17.933
Search below.

240
17:18.016 --> 17:18.892
Yes, sir!

241
17:33.740 --> 17:35.242
My lord, are you all right?

242
17:35.826 --> 17:37.703
Yuri, Kakei.

243
17:40.998 --> 17:42.207
Lord Yukimura.

244
17:44.084 --> 17:45.419
We must leave at once.

245
17:46.044 --> 17:47.045
Can we get away?

246
17:48.881 --> 17:52.134
I'll disguise myself as Lord Yukimura and draw the enemy away.

247
17:53.427 --> 17:54.261
That could work.

248
17:55.929 --> 17:56.972
Lord Yukimura, please.

249
18:01.518 --> 18:03.270
Our comrades aren't all here yet.

250
18:05.063 --> 18:06.648
I won't leave anyone behind.

251
18:08.775 --> 18:10.110
Can I ask you something?

252
18:11.278 --> 18:13.822
Are all lords in this country like you?

253
18:15.073 --> 18:16.033
My lord is…

254
18:19.494 --> 18:20.621
one of a kind.

255
18:23.081 --> 18:26.168
But if we delay, the enemy will only grow in number.

256
18:27.252 --> 18:28.587
And Hanzo too…

257
18:30.881 --> 18:32.966
Let me wait here

258
18:34.384 --> 18:35.928
for half an hour.

259
18:53.946 --> 18:56.114
Hey, how much longer?

260
18:57.115 --> 18:58.909
We're almost there. After you.

261
19:00.118 --> 19:01.870
Please.

262
19:40.284 --> 19:42.077
Isa, Seikai.

263
19:42.661 --> 19:43.912
Thank goodness you're safe.

264
19:44.413 --> 19:47.040
Now it's just Nezu and Sasuke.

265
19:48.583 --> 19:50.877
Nezu was…

266
19:51.586 --> 19:54.589
He was with the enemy.

267
19:54.673 --> 19:56.049
He's probably heading here now.

268
19:57.926 --> 19:58.885
He has betrayed us?

269
19:59.469 --> 20:01.221
Lord Yukimura, as I suggested…

270
20:02.222 --> 20:03.390
I told you.

271
20:03.473 --> 20:06.184
We're not like the Tokugawa.

272
20:06.268 --> 20:08.603
Our bonds can also be our weakness.

273
20:09.479 --> 20:10.814
Saizo is right.

274
20:11.440 --> 20:13.734
If our lord falls, it's all over.

275
20:14.735 --> 20:16.987
For us and the Toyotomi.

276
20:18.322 --> 20:19.197
Lord Yukimura.

277
20:21.450 --> 20:23.410
It's not been half an hour yet, has it?

278
20:26.580 --> 20:27.831
All right!

279
20:27.914 --> 20:29.207
In times like these…

280
20:30.125 --> 20:31.168
let's eat while we wait.

281
20:32.377 --> 20:33.378
Right?

282
20:33.462 --> 20:34.463
Come on, Saizo.

283
20:40.344 --> 20:42.554
Hey. What's taking so long?

284
20:43.055 --> 20:45.807
Sorry. Looks like I got a little lost.

285
20:47.684 --> 20:48.643
Lord Tsuge.

286
20:49.478 --> 20:51.271
I find this man suspicious.

287
20:51.938 --> 20:54.691
Did you trick me?

288
20:55.317 --> 20:57.903
Of course not.

289
20:59.154 --> 21:01.198
Something's fishy.

290
21:01.782 --> 21:04.534
Damn it… I've got no choice.

291
21:06.161 --> 21:07.454
Ninja art…

292
21:07.537 --> 21:09.247
There's Lord Yukimura!

293
21:13.627 --> 21:16.129
You think you'd get away with such a cheap trick?

294
21:18.048 --> 21:19.674
Yeah, figured as much.

295
21:23.345 --> 21:24.679
Four-two, even.

296
21:25.347 --> 21:27.516
Guess my luck's run out.

297
21:30.060 --> 21:32.312
Move! Move, move!

298
21:32.396 --> 21:33.480
Sasuke.

299
21:40.487 --> 21:42.906
Sasuke! What are you doing?

300
21:43.740 --> 21:44.825
I was testing it.

301
21:47.661 --> 21:49.746
This marks the 30-ken distance.

302
21:51.665 --> 21:53.083
-Let's go. -Right!

303
21:55.794 --> 21:57.462
So my dice were wrong after all…

304
22:06.430 --> 22:10.016
Half an hour has passed.

305
22:22.529 --> 22:23.947
No way…

306
22:29.494 --> 22:31.580
Found you.

307
22:39.212 --> 22:40.672
Did I sound like him?

308
22:40.755 --> 22:42.465
Sasuke! Nezu!

309
22:42.549 --> 22:44.843
Don't scare us like that!

310
22:44.926 --> 22:45.760
You…

311
22:45.844 --> 22:47.345
That's nothing to joke about!

312
22:47.429 --> 22:49.890
Nezu, didn't you defect to the enemy?

313
22:49.973 --> 22:52.017
Yeah, it was all an act.

314
22:52.601 --> 22:54.060
-What? -Seikai.

315
22:54.144 --> 22:55.812
I need to ask you for a favor later.

316
23:00.442 --> 23:02.986
Welcome back, both of you.

317
23:04.821 --> 23:06.489
Eat up. I saved you some food.

318
23:08.491 --> 23:09.492
Much obliged.

319
23:13.663 --> 23:16.583
All right. Let's go.

320
23:17.459 --> 23:19.211
Go where?

321
23:19.294 --> 23:20.712
The river, of course.

322
23:20.795 --> 23:23.089
I'll jump across that river myself.

323
23:23.173 --> 23:25.258
I just have to tie the rope to the other bank, right?

324
23:25.342 --> 23:27.594
There's no way you can do that.

325
23:29.596 --> 23:31.389
Saizo will act as a decoy.

326
23:31.473 --> 23:33.308
Use that chance to circle around.

327
23:33.391 --> 23:34.643
No.

328
23:34.726 --> 23:37.270
I hate being ordered around.

329
23:38.688 --> 23:41.441
Besides, wasn't this your plan?

330
23:42.067 --> 23:43.902
I thought it was a good one.

331
23:44.861 --> 23:46.655
Have a little faith in yourself.

332
23:47.906 --> 23:48.823
Don't worry.

333
23:49.699 --> 23:50.867
I can do it.

334
23:55.038 --> 23:56.539
Lord Yukimura.

335
24:04.089 --> 24:05.006
I'm…

336
24:07.384 --> 24:08.635
I'm staying here.

337
24:20.605 --> 24:21.856
Why didn't you say anything?

338
24:21.940 --> 24:23.233
Seikai!

339
24:26.444 --> 24:29.030
We have to get to Osaka quickly!

340
24:29.114 --> 24:30.115
Let's leave…

341
24:31.658 --> 24:33.410
I can't cross like this.

342
24:33.493 --> 24:35.787
Lord Yukimura, let me be the decoy, then.

343
24:35.870 --> 24:37.580
Don't worry about me.

344
24:38.999 --> 24:40.917
I'll only hold you back anyway.

345
24:46.923 --> 24:48.800
I'm counting on you to protect Lord Yukimura.

346
24:52.304 --> 24:53.680
What do you think

347
24:55.682 --> 24:57.475
we've endured 14 years for?

348
25:07.152 --> 25:08.528
Do not worry, my lord.

349
25:10.488 --> 25:11.781
I'll make it through.

350
25:18.204 --> 25:20.081
I suppose that's our only option.

351
25:25.003 --> 25:27.589
Damn it. Why do you always give up so easily?

352
25:28.840 --> 25:32.927
If that's what you call loyalty, then it's bullshit.

353
25:34.512 --> 25:35.847
That's enough.

354
25:36.765 --> 25:38.808
Don't trample on Yuri's resolve.

355
25:43.980 --> 25:45.565
I'll carry her across.

356
25:51.654 --> 25:53.990
There's no way you can do that.

357
25:54.074 --> 25:55.033
I can.

358
25:56.451 --> 25:57.994
Don't give up before we've even tried.

359
26:00.914 --> 26:02.540
Sasuke's right.

360
26:05.293 --> 26:10.256
Everyone here, except Lord Yukimura, suspected him.

361
26:11.257 --> 26:15.845
And none of us thought Sasuke would ever come back, either.

362
26:16.596 --> 26:20.058
But look at them. They're both back.

363
26:22.477 --> 26:23.645
That's right!

364
26:25.271 --> 26:26.648
I think it's too soon

365
26:27.941 --> 26:29.109
to give up.

366
26:35.657 --> 26:37.033
Double fives. Even.

367
26:37.742 --> 26:39.202
Not a bad roll.

368
26:40.495 --> 26:42.622
My lord, what are your orders?

369
26:49.796 --> 26:50.880
We are…

370
26:51.881 --> 26:53.758
all going to Osaka.

371
26:56.094 --> 26:57.762
No one gets left behind.

372
27:05.854 --> 27:06.855
Yes, my lord.

373
27:30.545 --> 27:31.546
Lord Hanzo!

374
27:31.629 --> 27:32.922
What of Yukimura?

375
27:33.006 --> 27:34.132
My apologies!

376
27:34.716 --> 27:35.967
But rest assured.

377
27:36.050 --> 27:38.303
We're doing everything we can to find him.

378
27:38.386 --> 27:41.014
We'll bring him in shortly.

379
27:41.097 --> 27:42.599
Don't get the wrong idea.

380
27:43.850 --> 27:46.686
This is a direct order from the Ogosho himself.

381
27:47.729 --> 27:49.481
You know what happens if you let him escape…

382
27:50.940 --> 27:51.941
don't you?

383
27:54.986 --> 27:56.112
I'll bring him in at once.

384
27:58.281 --> 28:00.366
Sasuke, I'm counting on you.

385
28:00.450 --> 28:01.284
Leave it to me.

386
28:01.951 --> 28:03.661
Sarutobi Sasuke's on the job.

387
28:07.790 --> 28:09.125
He's been alive all this time.

388
28:13.129 --> 28:14.589
Do you remember that promise?

389
28:15.340 --> 28:18.760
When we get to Osaka, how about we go eat konpeito together?

390
28:20.512 --> 28:22.055
Konpeito, then.

391
28:22.680 --> 28:24.933
I'll even join you for dango.

392
28:26.392 --> 28:28.436
Hold on tight.

393
28:47.288 --> 28:48.248
That far?

394
28:53.211 --> 28:54.462
This feels great!

395
28:54.546 --> 28:55.588
Watch where you're going!

396
29:11.312 --> 29:12.897
That was close.

397
29:15.066 --> 29:16.067
You okay?

398
29:27.495 --> 29:28.872
Thank goodness!

399
29:28.955 --> 29:30.582
Well done, Sasuke.

400
29:47.056 --> 29:48.725
Almost there, old man!

401
30:09.871 --> 30:12.248
You saved us, Okuni.

402
30:13.791 --> 30:14.751
Now, it's just…

403
30:25.053 --> 30:27.305
Brother, do your best.

404
30:30.808 --> 30:33.311
Hurry, Isa! The enemy's coming!

405
30:39.776 --> 30:40.944
I can't do it!

406
30:41.819 --> 30:43.279
I can't!

407
30:43.363 --> 30:46.407
Get a hold of yourself! You can do it!

408
30:46.991 --> 30:49.494
Sasuke's right! Come on!

409
30:52.789 --> 30:54.082
Isa!

410
30:55.208 --> 30:57.251
Isa! You'll be okay!

411
30:57.335 --> 30:58.962
-You'll be okay! -Brother…

412
30:59.045 --> 31:00.463
Isa!

413
31:01.881 --> 31:03.675
Isa!

414
31:06.177 --> 31:07.136
Keep going!

415
31:13.476 --> 31:14.519
Brother!

416
31:33.955 --> 31:35.832
You're all right! Hurry up!

417
31:40.169 --> 31:41.170
Kakei. Mochizuki.

418
31:41.254 --> 31:42.255
Right!

419
31:43.965 --> 31:46.592
-Hurry up! -Kakei, now!

420
31:46.676 --> 31:48.136
Shoot now!

421
31:56.310 --> 31:57.353
Come on, pull!

422
31:57.437 --> 31:58.688
Heave-ho!

423
31:59.856 --> 32:01.024
Heave-ho!

424
32:02.275 --> 32:03.526
Heave-ho!

425
32:10.825 --> 32:12.076
What the hell are you doing?

426
32:12.160 --> 32:13.953
We did it!

427
32:14.037 --> 32:15.747
Sorry to keep you waiting!

428
32:15.830 --> 32:17.457
I thought I was a goner.

429
32:21.002 --> 32:22.086
I told you all,

430
32:22.837 --> 32:24.213
didn't I?

431
32:24.297 --> 32:26.090
A bundle of threads can never be cut.

432
32:43.107 --> 32:45.985
Let's go. To Osaka!

433
32:51.741 --> 32:52.867
Lord Hanzo.

434
32:54.494 --> 32:55.787
So that ninja is…

435
32:58.915 --> 33:00.124
Sasuke.

436
33:04.712 --> 33:06.798
I'll make you pay!

437
33:16.557 --> 33:19.060
-Are you all right? -I'm fine.

438
33:21.145 --> 33:23.231
What do you make of him?

439
33:25.149 --> 33:26.317
I don't know.

440
33:27.318 --> 33:28.694
He's nothing like us.

441
33:29.487 --> 33:31.697
Yeah, that's true.

442
33:32.657 --> 33:38.079
But he'll do whatever it takes to forge a path where none exists.

443
33:39.789 --> 33:43.209
The world to come will need men like him.

444
33:44.502 --> 33:45.670
That's my feeling.

445
33:47.672 --> 33:50.133
Hey, how was my leap?

446
33:54.929 --> 33:56.013
Just a hunch, though.

447
34:02.937 --> 34:04.522
All right, everyone!

448
34:04.605 --> 34:07.400
We're almost there!

449
34:07.483 --> 34:10.194
Found you.

450
34:10.278 --> 34:13.281
Come on, Sasuke. Please stop…

451
34:20.788 --> 34:22.123
They're here!

452
34:22.874 --> 34:24.917
Lord Daisuke, stand back!

453
34:26.169 --> 34:29.172
Bind, Secure, Conceal, Ironize.

454
34:42.226 --> 34:43.311
What a pain…

455
34:43.811 --> 34:47.064
I'll kill the first one who comes at me.

456
34:52.737 --> 34:55.031
How do you like it?

457
34:55.114 --> 34:58.326
What you just took was a powerful laxative I made.

458
34:59.619 --> 35:00.620
What?

459
35:00.703 --> 35:02.830
The main ingredient is deer droppings.

460
35:04.749 --> 35:06.584
This is what you use, right?

461
35:08.836 --> 35:11.756
So this medicine is the secret to your strength after all.

462
35:20.473 --> 35:23.392
You said ninja don't care about their comrades.

463
35:24.518 --> 35:25.645
Well, we do!

464
35:26.229 --> 35:28.856
We're nothing like you!

465
35:30.274 --> 35:31.400
Flame Release!

466
36:12.316 --> 36:13.526
BOMB

467
36:36.173 --> 36:37.717
You had to steal my moment.

468
36:37.800 --> 36:39.635
You took too long. That was close.

469
36:39.719 --> 36:42.263
You were struggling too.

470
36:45.683 --> 36:47.810
If those two could just get in sync…

471
36:47.893 --> 36:48.811
Yeah.

472
36:55.901 --> 36:58.446
We are the Sanada Ten Braves.

473
36:58.529 --> 37:00.865
When our ten strengths unite as one,

474
37:01.449 --> 37:04.118
no foe, however mighty, can break us.

475
37:06.537 --> 37:08.080
You underestimated our bond.

476
37:09.582 --> 37:10.916
That was your undoing.

477
37:12.752 --> 37:15.212
You'll pay for Unno's death.

478
37:28.476 --> 37:30.853
Damn it. The bastard just won't stay down.

479
37:31.729 --> 37:33.647
I can't believe he still had that in him.

480
37:33.731 --> 37:34.940
But we won!

481
37:35.024 --> 37:37.985
We actually beat Tsuge! Amazing!

482
37:40.654 --> 37:42.948
You all did well.

483
37:43.032 --> 37:43.866
Yes, my lord.

484
37:55.711 --> 37:58.964
I mean, what's with this whole Sanada Ten Braves thing?

485
38:00.174 --> 38:01.425
Don't be embarrassed.

486
38:02.009 --> 38:02.968
I'm not embarrassed.

487
38:08.099 --> 38:11.102
OSAKA CASTLE

488
38:14.271 --> 38:15.731
Open the gates!

489
38:17.108 --> 38:22.238
Lord Sanada Yukimura has arrived!

490
38:24.782 --> 38:26.492
A welcoming feast, perhaps?

491
38:26.575 --> 38:28.244
A feast?

492
38:28.327 --> 38:29.495
Of course!

493
38:30.162 --> 38:33.124
The hero who's come to save them in their hour of need is here!

494
38:34.208 --> 38:35.167
A feast, huh?

495
38:40.798 --> 38:41.841
Who are these men?

496
38:42.967 --> 38:43.843
We are…

497
38:45.219 --> 38:46.887
the peerless ninja squad,

498
38:47.555 --> 38:49.306
-the Sanada Ten Braves-- -Please leave.

499
38:50.266 --> 38:52.101
Ninja aren't allowed in the castle.

500
38:52.810 --> 38:53.644
What?

501
38:55.312 --> 38:57.189
You let Yukimura escape?

502
38:57.273 --> 38:59.358
My apologies, my lord.

503
39:00.818 --> 39:02.027
Atone for it with your life!

504
39:04.864 --> 39:05.698
Yes, my lord.

505
39:05.781 --> 39:06.866
Hold on.

506
39:07.825 --> 39:10.619
It's not all bad.

507
39:12.246 --> 39:16.375
Yukimura entering Osaka Castle gives us the perfect pretext for war.

508
39:17.168 --> 39:20.045
Now we have grounds to attack the Toyotomi.

509
39:20.754 --> 39:23.591
The people of the realm will accept it.

510
39:24.842 --> 39:26.969
Thank you, my lord! Next time, I'll get him!

511
39:27.761 --> 39:28.804
Still,

512
39:29.388 --> 39:32.308
you couldn't kill a single one of Sanada's ninja?

513
39:33.642 --> 39:36.312
Perhaps it's time to retrain your men.

514
39:37.229 --> 39:38.522
Quite right.

515
39:45.905 --> 39:46.822
Here you are.

516
39:53.621 --> 39:54.580
Lord Hanzo…

517
39:55.623 --> 39:56.499
You fool.

518
40:02.046 --> 40:03.797
I, Sanada Yukimura,

519
40:04.924 --> 40:07.843
have arrived, though belatedly.

520
40:08.928 --> 40:10.638
You've come at last.

521
40:10.721 --> 40:11.555
ONO HARUNAGA

522
40:11.639 --> 40:15.017
Your journey from Kudoyama must have been arduous.

523
40:16.352 --> 40:18.854
After coming all this way,

524
40:18.938 --> 40:21.106
why do we have to hide in a place like this?

525
40:22.608 --> 40:23.859
I'm starving.

526
40:25.152 --> 40:27.905
So much for a feast. Got my hopes up for nothing.

527
40:28.781 --> 40:30.991
Even as Lord Yukimura's retainers,

528
40:31.075 --> 40:33.452
we're still just ninja to them.

529
40:35.037 --> 40:37.665
Are ninja really so hated?

530
40:38.499 --> 40:41.877
Shady outsiders who use underhanded tactics.

531
40:42.628 --> 40:45.548
That's how they see us, especially the samurai.

532
40:47.716 --> 40:49.093
I see.

533
40:49.176 --> 40:51.971
Lord Daisuke, why are you here too?

534
40:53.430 --> 40:55.516
There's nothing for me to do in the castle.

535
41:03.315 --> 41:04.692
I want to be as strong…

536
41:07.111 --> 41:08.195
as a ninja!

537
41:12.241 --> 41:13.117
So…

538
41:14.785 --> 41:17.246
All right. Come with me.

539
41:17.955 --> 41:19.790
First, we gather intelligence.

540
41:19.873 --> 41:21.625
Let's see how the war council is going.

541
41:22.585 --> 41:23.586
Yes!

542
41:23.669 --> 41:26.213
I'd like to see Lady Yodo too. Come on.

543
41:26.964 --> 41:28.007
Understood!

544
41:29.008 --> 41:30.009
Still…

545
41:30.759 --> 41:33.679
you've brought a mere ten men with you.

546
41:34.346 --> 41:36.849
And most of them are ninja.

547
41:37.975 --> 41:43.689
So the Sanada clan owed its strength to your father, Lord Masayuki.

548
41:44.273 --> 41:47.151
There's nothing less trustworthy than a ninja.

549
41:47.234 --> 41:48.485
ODA URAKUSAI

550
41:48.569 --> 41:52.281
I'd sooner deal with the ronin.

551
41:52.364 --> 41:53.532
GOTO MATABE

552
41:59.830 --> 42:01.206
Acting all high and mighty.

553
42:01.915 --> 42:03.042
Who do they think they are?

554
42:04.376 --> 42:05.753
Without further ado,

555
42:06.420 --> 42:10.007
what plan do you propose?

556
42:10.758 --> 42:11.842
A plan?

557
42:11.925 --> 42:13.427
They don't have one.

558
42:14.136 --> 42:15.304
I'm Goto Matabe.

559
42:16.013 --> 42:19.016
These fools don't know the first thing about war.

560
42:19.099 --> 42:20.309
How dare you!

561
42:21.018 --> 42:23.312
A mere ronin should know his place.

562
42:24.355 --> 42:27.691
Then allow me to lay out my plan.

563
42:32.529 --> 42:35.032
KAMEYAMA

564
42:35.115 --> 42:37.993
Ieyasu will soon enter Nijo Castle

565
42:38.077 --> 42:40.079
to launch an attack on Osaka.

566
42:41.914 --> 42:46.377
We'll strike Fushimi before its forces are ready.

567
42:47.211 --> 42:48.128
KYOTO FUSHIMI

568
42:48.212 --> 42:49.588
Using that as our foothold,

569
42:50.756 --> 42:55.886
we'll storm Nijo Castle, and before Hidetada's forces arrive…

570
42:57.429 --> 42:59.932
we'll take Ieyasu's head.

571
43:02.685 --> 43:04.436
With Ieyasu dead,

572
43:04.520 --> 43:08.357
the warlords loyal to the Tokugawa will have no reason to fight.

573
43:09.441 --> 43:12.444
They will readily switch sides and join us.

574
43:12.528 --> 43:13.821
KYOTO OSAKA NARA

575
43:13.904 --> 43:15.656
We'll bring them over to our side

576
43:16.448 --> 43:19.868
and use their troops to strike Hidetada from behind.

577
43:21.537 --> 43:24.039
That will win us the war.

578
43:25.666 --> 43:27.543
Once Hidetada's forces arrive,

579
43:28.502 --> 43:30.546
the enemy will number over 100,000.

580
43:31.755 --> 43:33.632
We mustn't let this chance slip away.

581
43:43.809 --> 43:46.437
That's incredible. Just as I'd expect.

582
43:47.813 --> 43:48.647
Right.

583
43:48.731 --> 43:49.940
It's settled, then.

584
43:52.067 --> 43:53.402
Lady Yodo.

585
44:00.033 --> 44:01.034
Nobushige.

586
44:02.536 --> 44:03.495
Lady Yodo.

587
44:04.371 --> 44:06.457
I go by Yukimura now.

588
44:07.750 --> 44:10.753
I apologize for my late arrival.

589
44:13.756 --> 44:15.090
I, Sanada Yukimura,

590
44:16.508 --> 44:18.051
have arrived.

591
44:24.600 --> 44:26.727
So that's Lady Yodo.

592
44:32.065 --> 44:33.484
Nobushige,

593
44:33.567 --> 44:36.570
why didn't you come to me at once?

594
44:37.488 --> 44:39.239
The Tokugawa forces are closing in.

595
44:39.948 --> 44:42.534
Every moment counts, so we must hold the war council first.

596
44:42.618 --> 44:45.829
That can wait.

597
44:45.913 --> 44:47.456
Oh my…

598
44:47.539 --> 44:49.541
"That can wait"?

599
44:50.334 --> 44:51.210
But…

600
44:52.252 --> 44:54.630
If the enemy attacks, we'll just hold out here.

601
44:55.672 --> 44:58.800
This is a magnificent castle built by the Taiko himself.

602
44:59.801 --> 45:01.637
It can never fall.

603
45:02.804 --> 45:04.765
Isn't that right?

604
45:05.349 --> 45:06.433
Yes.

605
45:08.018 --> 45:11.313
Osaka Castle is certainly well-fortified.

606
45:11.855 --> 45:12.731
But…

607
45:13.357 --> 45:17.152
holding out under siege only works when we can count on reinforcements.

608
45:18.320 --> 45:21.031
Even if we hold out for a while, sooner or later…

609
45:21.114 --> 45:22.741
A sortie is out of the question!

610
45:23.992 --> 45:27.996
What if anything happened to Hideyori?

611
45:29.790 --> 45:32.334
Holding out here is our only option.

612
45:33.752 --> 45:34.711
This council is over.

613
45:38.257 --> 45:39.383
Lord Hideyori!

614
45:40.300 --> 45:43.303
What do you think, Lord Hideyori?

615
46:11.540 --> 46:12.583
As my mother…

616
46:13.792 --> 46:15.043
commands.

617
46:15.127 --> 46:16.169
TOYOTOMI HIDEYORI

618
46:16.920 --> 46:17.963
What is going on?

619
46:29.016 --> 46:31.226
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

620
46:31.310 --> 46:33.270
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
